sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor U as Cook
  participant API as marketmate-api
  participant PG as PostgreSQL
  participant YT as YouTube
  participant LLM as OpenAI
  participant R as Redis
  participant M as Google Places

  U->>API: POST /api/process-video<br/>{url, lat, lng}
  API->>API: ParseVideoID(url)
  Note right of API: Handles ?si= and &t= query junk.<br/>The original sliced the last 11<br/>characters and panicked on short input.

  rect rgb(248, 250, 252)
    Note over API,LLM: The expensive half — cached permanently
    API->>PG: SELECT transcript WHERE video_id = $1
    alt cold video
      PG-->>API: miss
      API->>YT: fetch transcript
      YT-->>API: transcript
      API->>PG: INSERT INTO videos
      API->>LLM: extract ingredients<br/>(prompt + model → version fingerprint)
      LLM-->>API: structured ingredients
      API->>PG: INSERT INTO extractions<br/>(video_id, model_version, ingredients)
      Note right of PG: A transcript never changes, so this<br/>never expires. The version fingerprint<br/>is what invalidates it — edit the prompt<br/>and the next request re-extracts.
    else already seen
      PG-->>API: transcript + extraction
      Note right of API: No network call, no LLM spend.<br/>This is why the second person to<br/>try a recipe gets it instantly.
    end
  end

  rect rgb(248, 250, 252)
    Note over API,M: The perishable half — short TTL
    API->>API: geohash(lat, lng, precision 5) ≈ 5 km cell
    API->>R: GET stores:{video}:{geohash}
    alt cache hit
      R-->>API: store list
    else cold cell
      R-->>API: miss
      API->>M: nearby stores for the ingredient set<br/>(batched, not one call per ingredient)
      M-->>API: stores + distances
      API->>R: SETEX 15m
      Note right of R: Stores open, close and move.<br/>Unlike a transcript this genuinely<br/>goes stale, so it keeps a TTL.
    end
  end

  API-->>U: recipe + ingredients + nearby stores<br/>each carrying its provenance
  Note over U,API: Provenance travels with the data: a fixture result is<br/>labelled simulated at every layer, so a demo can never be<br/>mistaken for a live lookup.
